+/* ---------- Relay request 18: MyMISMO's live files in Amazon S3 (Jonna, Nov 27, 2026) ----------
+ * GitHub allows one account about 500 saves an hour; a summit with hundreds of people on MyMISMO needs thousands. When
+ * MYMISMO_BUCKET names a private S3 bucket (versioning on, so every earlier copy is kept, like GitHub's history), the
+ * files MyMISMO changes all day are kept there instead of in its GitHub repository: sign-in codes and profiles,
+ * messages, reports, headshots, check-ins, Who I Met and touchpoints, summit photos, alert phones and the alerts sent,
+ * and Trivia plays, boards and contacts. The question bank, Trivia settings and MISMO Media's news alerts stay on GitHub.
+ * Every route reads and writes exactly as before (readFile and updateRepoJson pick the store), each save is checked
+ * against the copy it changed (S3 conditional writes, like GitHub's sha), and a file not yet in S3 is read from GitHub
+ * once, so nothing is lost on the switch. Meeting Trackers and Member 360 read scan/ from GitHub, so a scheduled run
+ * (EventBridge, every 15 minutes, input {"mymismoMirror": true}) copies the scan/ files that changed to GitHub.
+ * With MYMISMO_BUCKET unset, nothing changes. */
